        "clinical_uncertainties[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "speaker_role": "patient",
      "transcript_text": "Hm. It was either the end of last month or earlier than that. I couldn't tell you the date.",
      "start_timestamp": "00:37",
      "end_timestamp": "00:47",
      "supports": [
        "symptoms[0]",
        "clinical_uncertainties[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "Can you describe it a bit more for me? How strong it is, what the pattern is, what helps.",
      "start_timestamp": "00:48",
      "end_timestamp": "00:57",
      "supports": [
        "symptoms[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "speaker_role": "patient",
      "transcript_text": "It happens all the time. Pretty mild, if I'm being honest. I'm not great at remembering details, so bear with me.",
      "start_timestamp": "00:58",
      "end_timestamp": "01:08",
      "supports": [
        "symptoms[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "Is there anything else with it?",
      "start_timestamp": "01:09",
      "end_timestamp": "01:11",
      "supports": [
        "symptoms[0]",
        "symptoms[1]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "speaker_role": "patient",
      "transcript_text": "Um, it usually comes with cramping tummy pain. I've also been feeling dehydrated.",
      "start_timestamp": "01:12",
      "end_timestamp": "01:19",
      "supports": [
        "symptoms[0]",
        "symptoms[1]",
        "symptoms[2]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "Tell me a bit more about it: how bad it gets, how often, and whether anything makes it better or worse.",
      "start_timestamp": "01:20",
      "end_timestamp": "01:29",
      "supports": [
        "symptoms[2]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "speaker_role": "patient",
      "transcript_text": "I get some relief from drinking water. Mostly severe. I didn't want to bother you but it keeps coming back. Yeah, with cramping tummy pain, it's a few times a day.",
      "start_timestamp": "01:30",
      "end_timestamp": "01:47",
      "supports": [
        "symptoms[1]",
        "symptoms[2]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "What about a low fever, have you noticed that?",
      "start_timestamp": "01:48",
      "end_timestamp": "01:52",
      "supports": [
        "symptoms[3]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "speaker_role": "patient",
      "transcript_text": "Yes, about the same, five days. With low fever, about a four out of ten. Honestly, all the time.",
